# Security & Privacy

## Threat model

Personal local overlay — not a hosted service. Still: don't expand attack surface unnecessarily.

## Memory access

- Read-only external process memory. No writes to game process. No code injection.
- Require user to run overlay alongside game; admin only when Windows blocks cross-process read.

## Network

- API binds `localhost` only (`127.0.0.1`). No telemetry, no cloud upload of game state by default.
- Optional price APIs (e.g. poe.ninja) fetch **public** price data — never send account credentials.

## Data exposure

- `/state` exposes in-game positions/entities to local browser — expected for dashboard.
- Don't log player names, passwords, or full memory dumps to disk in release paths.
- Crash logs: minimal context in `logs/poe2radar-crash.log`.

## Input

- `SendInput` only for gated auto-flask. Don't add keyloggers or global hooks beyond hotkey poll.
